// UnusedExportCheck — E3092 / E3093 / E3094: a declaration more widely visible than its uses require.
//
// Three diagnostics, one walk (`specs/unused-export.md`):
//   • E3092 `semanticUnusedExportedSymbol`  — an `export` decl no file outside its declaring one names
//   • E3093 `semanticExportableAsModule`    — an `export` decl named only inside its declaring subtree
//   • E3094 `semanticUnusedModuleSymbol`    — a `module` decl no file outside its declaring one names
//
// ⭐⭐ **`public` IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS PASS EXISTS AT ALL, AND IT IS WHY THERE IS NO STDLIB
// CARVE-OUT HERE.** The family was implemented once before (2026-08-03) and REMOVED IN FULL by user
// ruling: *"exporting something effectively makes it part of a public api. it could be a shared module
// that doesn't happen to use that symbol in this particular app. that doesn't mean it is dead."* That
// objection is correct, and it is about a CONFLATION rather than about the lint — `export` was being
// read as a claim about USE when it states only VISIBILITY. `public` separates the two:
//   • `export` — other files may see this, AND I expect this program to use it. Audited here.
//   • `public` — this is API surface. Exempt, because "no caller in THIS compilation" is not "dead".
//
// ⇒ **v1 needs TWO stdlib exemptions ON THE SEED and this pass needs NEITHER.** `maxon-selfhosted` skips
// the whole pass for the stdlib's own compile (`PassPipeline:321`) AND filters every stdlib declaration out
// of the seed by PATH when compiling user code (`UnusedExportCheck:106`), whose comment says exactly why:
// *"Without this filter the pass would emit E3092 against every stdlib typealias the user happens not
// to mention."* Every one of `stdlib/`'s 680 exported declarations is `public` now, so they fall out at
// the `isProgramWideTier`-and-not-`global` test below like any other author's API surface would. The
// exemption became a fact the author states instead of a path this pass has to know about.
//
// ⚠ **THE PASS DOES KNOW ABOUT THE LIBRARY IN ONE PLACE, AND IT IS THE READER SIDE, WHICH NEITHER v1
// EXEMPTION COVERS** — `noteRead` refuses to let a library file be credited with a reference to an AUTHOR's
// declaration, because a monomorphized `Array with Item` body carries `stdlib/Array.maxon` as its source
// file and cannot possibly have named `Item`. The rule and what it cost are stated in full there.
//
// ⚠ **WHAT IS STILL AUDITED IN `stdlib/`: its six `module` declarations** (all in `String.maxon`).
// That is deliberate — `module` is the marked, narrower tier there, and E3094 is exactly the signal its
// author wants if a door stops being reached. MEASURED at the time of writing: all six are named from
// outside `String.maxon`, so none fires.

// ── Gates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ⭐ **THE STRUCTURAL GATE IS THE PIPELINE'S, NOT THIS PASS'S — AND THAT IS STRICTLY STRONGER THAN v1'S.**
// v1 opens with `projectHasStructuralErrors`, skipping the audit when any lexer (1xxx), parser (2xxx) or
// IR-stage (4xxx) diagnostic exists, so that a half-resolved reader cannot produce spurious findings. Here
// the schedule already guarantees it: `PassPipeline.run` throws the moment ANY pass reports a diagnostic,
// and this pass is scheduled after `semanticCheck`, so reaching it means the project's diagnostic list is
// empty. Re-testing it here would be a second answer to a question the driver has already answered.

// A one-file program's exports are its public surface and nothing outside can name them, so every
// `export` in one would be E3092 and the diagnostic would be noise rather than a finding. v1 short-circuits
// the same way (`UnusedExportCheck:893-899`).
//
// ⚠ **IT COUNTS USER FILES, NOT SOURCE PATHS.** `project.db.sourcePaths` holds every stdlib file the loader
// pulled in, so the raw count is in the dozens for a one-file program and the gate would never fire. v1's
// `sourcePaths` excludes the stdlib, which is what makes its `< 2` test mean what it says; shv2's does not,
// so the stdlib half is filtered here and the question stays "how many files did the AUTHOR write?".
let MinimumUserFilesToAudit = 2

// ── What is seeded ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Which namespace a tracked declaration lives in. A reference names a FUNCTION, a TYPE or a top-level
// BINDING, and the three cannot be confused for one another at a use site, so they are keyed apart.
enum TrackedDeclKind
	trackedFunction
	trackedType
	trackedBinding
end 'TrackedDeclKind'

// One `export`/`module` declaration and the widest scope anything has been seen to read it from.
//
// ⚠ **THE TWO BITS ARE MONOTONIC AND ARE NEVER NARROWED.** A declaration read from two files is read
// from the wider of them, so every `note` widens or does nothing; a `set` that could clear one would make
// the answer depend on which reader was visited last.
type TrackedDecl
	export var kind as TrackedDeclKind
	// The key a reference is matched against — a function's compiled name, a type's name, or a binding's
	// name. NOT the display spelling: `displayName` is what the message prints.
	export var key as ByteArray
	export var displayName as String
	// The word the message calls this declaration: "function", "type", "typealias", "constant", "variable".
	// Taken from the reference compiler's own vocabulary (`UnusedExportCheck.emitOne*`), which the spec's
	// expectations quote verbatim.
	export var noun as String
	export var visibility as Visibility
	export var declFilePath as FilePath
	export var declModuleDirectory as String
	export var nameLine as LineNumber
	export var nameColumn as ColumnNumber
	export var sawOutsideFile as bool
	export var sawOutsideModule as bool

	export static function create(kind TrackedDeclKind, key ByteArray, displayName String, noun String, visibility Visibility, declFilePath FilePath, declModuleDirectory String, nameLine LineNumber, nameColumn ColumnNumber) returns TrackedDecl
		return Self{kind: kind, key: key, displayName: displayName, noun: noun, visibility: visibility, declFilePath: declFilePath, declModuleDirectory: declModuleDirectory, nameLine: nameLine, nameColumn: nameColumn, sawOutsideFile: false, sawOutsideModule: false}
	end 'create'
end 'TrackedDecl'

typealias TrackedDeclArray = Array with TrackedDecl
typealias TrackedDeclIndex = int(0 to u64.max)

// ⛔⛔ **A BARE NAME IS NOT A DECLARATION'S IDENTITY, AND KEYING THIS BY ONE PANICKED.** Two files in
// DIFFERENT DIRECTORIES may each declare `type NsDeep` or `function pick` — that is what a namespace is
// FOR, and `specs-shv2/namespace-qualified-resolution.md` is thirty cases about it. The index was a
// `Map with (ByteArray, TrackedDeclIndex)`, so the second declaration's `insert` threw `keyAlreadyExists`
// and the pass aborted the compile: MEASURED by `scale-test`'s generated corpus, which emits a namespace
// ladder — and NOT by any of the 6,377 spec cases, because none of them declares a contested name in a
// program that also compiles clean.
//
// ⇒ One name maps to EVERY declaration wearing it, and a reference to that name credits all of them.
// That OVER-approximates where two namespaces contest a name — a use of `alpha.pick` also credits
// `beta.pick` — and the direction is deliberate: crediting a reference too widely can only SUPPRESS a
// finding, while resolving to the wrong one of two claimants would report a live declaration as dead.
// Telling them apart needs the reader's own namespace precedence, which is `ProgramSignatures`' answer to
// give, not this pass's to re-derive.
typealias TrackedDeclIndexArray = Array with TrackedDeclIndex
typealias TrackedDeclIndexMap = Map with (ByteArray, TrackedDeclIndexArray)

// ⭐⭐ **EVERY STORED GLOBAL'S `.data` LABEL, MAPPED TO THE DECLARATION THAT OWNS IT.** A `globalAddr`
// op carries the LABEL and this seed is keyed by source NAME, so somewhere the two have to be joined —
// `noteGlobalLabel` is the one place that asks.
//
// ⚠⚠ **IT IS A MAP BECAUSE THE JOIN WAS A SCAN OF THE WHOLE DECLARATION ARENA AT EVERY `globalAddr`
// OP, AND THAT PRODUCT WAS THIS PASS'S SUPERLINEAR TERM.** Both of its factors DOUBLE per rung of the
// scaling ladder — the top-level `let`/`var` COUNT and the number of sites that read one — so the scan
// quadrupled while everything around it doubled. MEASURED, `phase:checkUnusedExports` CPU per doubling:
// x1.43 x1.58 x1.86 x2.28 x2.74, monotonic, against x2.00 for linear.
//
// ⛔ **AND THE MEMORY COLUMNS READ IT AS PERFECTLY LINEAR — x1.90 allocations, x1.89 bytes — because a
// scan step ALLOCATES NOTHING.** It copies a `TopLevelDecl`, which RETAINS six managed handles (its
// whole `TokenArray` among them) and releases them again, so the entire quadratic was refcount traffic.
// That is the class the CPU column was added to catch, and no other column of the instrument could see it.
typealias GlobalLabelIndexMap = Map with (ByteArray, TopLevelDeclIndex)

// The type names one transitive walk has already been through - what makes a self-referential type
// terminate. Per walk, not per pass: the answer depends on the READER file, so a pass-wide memo would
// credit the second reader with the first one's result.
typealias VisitedTypeNameSet = Set with ByteArray

// The LIBRARY's source files, keyed by the `FilePath.toString()` spelling every reader in this pass
// already carries. A SET and not a second walk, because `isStdlibSourceFile` resolves a path against the
// process's working directory — a `Directory.currentPath()` and two path builds — while `noteRead` asks
// the question at every credit.
typealias LibrarySourcePathSet = Set with String

// The author's files and the library's, told apart in ONE walk over `project.db.sourcePaths`. Both halves
// come from the same `isStdlibSourceFile` answer per path, so the two populations cannot come to
// disagree about a file the way two independently-filtered walks could.
type SourcePathSplit
	export let userFiles as FilePathArray
	export let libraryFiles as LibrarySourcePathSet

	export static function create(userFiles FilePathArray, libraryFiles LibrarySourcePathSet) returns SourcePathSplit
		return Self{userFiles: userFiles, libraryFiles: libraryFiles}
	end 'create'
end 'SourcePathSplit'

// The seed, plus the three by-name indexes a reference is resolved through. One array so emission order
// is DECLARATION order and therefore deterministic — a map iteration would make the diagnostic order an
// artifact of hashing, and two runs of one compiler must print the same bytes.
type TrackedDecls
	export var entries as TrackedDeclArray
	export var functionIndex as TrackedDeclIndexMap
	export var typeIndex as TrackedDeclIndexMap
	export var bindingIndex as TrackedDeclIndexMap
	// Which files are the library's — the one fact `noteRead` needs about a reader that neither the
	// reader's path nor the declaration carries. It rides here rather than as a fourth reader parameter
	// threaded through every `note*` because it is a property of the PROGRAM and not of any one credit.
	// Read by `noteRead` alone, which states the rule it serves.
	export let libraryFiles as LibrarySourcePathSet
	// The fourth index, and the only one keyed by something other than a source name — see
	// `GlobalLabelIndexMap`. It rides here for `libraryFiles`' reason: it is a property of the PROGRAM
	// rather than of any one credit, and threading it through every `note*` would say otherwise.
	export let globalLabels as GlobalLabelIndexMap

	export static function create(libraryFiles LibrarySourcePathSet, globalLabels GlobalLabelIndexMap) returns TrackedDecls
		return Self{entries: TrackedDeclArray.create(), functionIndex: TrackedDeclIndexMap.create(), typeIndex: TrackedDeclIndexMap.create(), bindingIndex: TrackedDeclIndexMap.create(), libraryFiles: libraryFiles, globalLabels: globalLabels}
	end 'create'

	export function add(decl TrackedDecl)
		let at = self.entries.count()
		self.entries.push(decl)
		match decl.kind 'kind'
			trackedFunction then self.indexUnder(self.functionIndex, key: decl.key, at: at)
			trackedType then self.indexUnder(self.typeIndex, key: decl.key, at: at)
			trackedBinding then self.indexUnder(self.bindingIndex, key: decl.key, at: at)
		end 'kind'
	end 'add'

	// `upsert`, not `insert`: a contested bare name is a legal program, not a collision — see
	// `TrackedDeclIndexMap`.
	// ⚠ The existing list is COPIED out before the write rather than pushed to in place: `get` hands back a
	// borrow of the map's own slot, and mutating the map through `upsert` while that borrow is live is
	// E3070. Built fresh, the borrow ends at the `if`.
	function indexUnder(index TrackedDeclIndexMap, key ByteArray, at TrackedDeclIndex)
		var claimants = TrackedDeclIndexArray.create()
		if let existing = try index.get(key) 'alreadyClaimed'
			claimants.append(existing)
		end 'alreadyClaimed'

		claimants.push(at)
		index.upsert(key, value: claimants)
	end 'indexUnder'

	export function at(index TrackedDeclIndex) returns TrackedDecl
		return try self.entries.get(index) otherwise panic("TrackedDecls.at: OOB at {index} — every index handed out is one this seed minted")
	end 'at'
end 'TrackedDecls'

// ── The pass ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export function checkUnusedExports(project Project, module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures) throws CompileError
	let sources = try splitSourcePaths(project)
	if sources.userFiles.count() < MinimumUserFilesToAudit 'tooFewFilesToHaveAnOutside'
		return
	end 'tooFewFilesToHaveAnOutside'

	var tracked = TrackedDecls.create(sources.libraryFiles, globalLabels: indexGlobalLabels(signatures))
	seedFunctions(module, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked)
	try seedTypes(project, signatures: signatures, userFiles: sources.userFiles, tracked: tracked)
	seedBindings(signatures, tracked: tracked)

	if tracked.entries.count() == 0 'nothingWiderThanAFile'
		return
	end 'nothingWiderThanAFile'

	collectReferences(module, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked)
	try collectFileTypeReferences(project, signatures: signatures, userFiles: sources.userFiles, tracked: tracked)
	emitDiagnostics(project, tracked: tracked)
end 'checkUnusedExports'

// The files the AUTHOR wrote, and the library's own — see `MinimumUserFilesToAudit` for why the gate above
// cannot count the library half, and `noteRead` for what the library half is used for.
function splitSourcePaths(project Project) returns SourcePathSplit throws CompileError
	var paths = FilePathArray.create()
	var libraryFiles = LibrarySourcePathSet.create()
	for path in project.db.sourcePaths 'eachFile'
		if isStdlibSourceFile(project, path: path) 'stdlibFile'
			libraryFiles.insert(path.toString())
			continue
		end 'stdlibFile'
		paths.push(path)
	end 'eachFile'

	return SourcePathSplit.create(paths, libraryFiles: libraryFiles)
end 'splitSourcePaths'

// One pass over the declaration arena, so `noteGlobalLabel` is a lookup and not a scan of it.
//
// ⚠ **FIRST WINS, exactly as the scan's `return` did.** Two declarations cannot share a `.data` label
// — it is minted from the storage key, which is what makes featA's `counter` and featB's `counter` two
// slots — but the tie is broken here anyway, so the answer can never come to depend on which of two
// claimants a map happened to keep.
function indexGlobalLabels(signatures ProgramSignatures) returns GlobalLabelIndexMap
	var labels = GlobalLabelIndexMap.create()
	for i in 0 upto signatures.topLevelDeclCount() 'eachDecl'
		let decl = signatures.declAt(i)
		// An immutable binding is INLINED at its use and has no slot to take the address of, so it has no
		// label at all — see `TopLevelDecl.dataLabel`.
		if not decl.hasStorage or labels.contains(decl.dataLabel) 'noSlotOrAlreadyClaimed'
			continue
		end 'noSlotOrAlreadyClaimed'

		labels.upsert(decl.dataLabel, value: i)
	end 'eachDecl'

	return labels
end 'indexGlobalLabels'

// ── Seeding ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Is this tier one the audit has anything to say about? `file` is already as narrow as a declaration
// gets, and `public` is the author's statement that "nobody here calls it" is not a finding.
function tierIsAudited(visibility Visibility) returns bool
	return match visibility 'tier'
		file gives false
		public gives false
		module gives true
		global gives true
	end 'tier'
end 'tierIsAudited'

// ⭐ **THE NAMES NO SOURCE LINE DECLARES.** A synthesized helper has no `export` an author could drop, so
// a finding about one is a finding about the compiler. v1 filters the same three shapes
// (`UnusedExportCheck.isSyntheticName`).
function isSynthesizedName(name ByteArray) returns bool
	let text = String.from(name)
	return text.startsWith("__") or text.contains("$closure_") or text.contains(".unionCases")
end 'isSynthesizedName'

// `main` is called by the entry stub and every module-init helper by the runtime, so neither has a
// source-level caller to find. v1 seeds the same set plus `project.livenessRoots`, which shv2 has no
// equivalent of — see `collectReferences` for what stands in its place.
function isEntrypointName(name ByteArray) returns bool
	return String.from(name).equals("main")
end 'isEntrypointName'

function seedFunctions(module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for func in module.functions 'eachFunc'
		if not tierIsAudited(func.visibility) 'narrowEnoughAlready'
			continue
		end 'narrowEnoughAlready'

		if func.sourceFilePath.toString().isEmpty() 'synthesizedFunction'
			continue
		end 'synthesizedFunction'

		if isSynthesizedName(func.name) or isEntrypointName(func.name) 'noSourceLevelCaller'
			continue
		end 'noSourceLevelCaller'

		// ⭐ **A METHOD TAKES ITS TIER FROM ITS DECLARING TYPE, SO THE TYPE OWNS THE DIAGNOSTIC.** Auditing
		// `Point.sum` on its own reports an internal helper of a public type as dead, and — worse — an
		// un-`export`ed method of a `module` type would report as E3093, advising a narrowing that is not
		// expressible. v1 states the identical rule and the identical reason
		// (`UnusedExportCheck.isMethodOnTrackedType`), and `specs/unused-export.md`'s
		// `error.unused-exported-type` PINS it: `LocalPoint` declares two exported methods and the case
		// expects exactly ONE diagnostic, about the type.
		if namesAMethodOnATrackedType(signatures, qualifiedName: func.name) 'theTypeOwnsIt'
			continue
		end 'theTypeOwnsIt'

		// ⭐ **THE MESSAGE SPELLS A FUNCTION WITH ITS NAMESPACE, AND THE SPELLING IS ASKED FOR RATHER THAN
		// BUILT.** `specs/unused-export.md` expects `'api.unusedHelper'`, not the bare registration name the
		// IR carries. `diagnosticCalleeSpelling` is the door every other visibility diagnostic already
		// spells a callee through — including the guard against re-qualifying a name that is already
		// qualified (`alpha.alpha.pick`), which a second copy of the join here would have got wrong.
		tracked.add(TrackedDecl.create(TrackedDeclKind.trackedFunction, key: func.name, displayName: String.from(signatures.diagnosticCalleeSpelling(func.name)), noun: "function", visibility: func.visibility, declFilePath: func.sourceFilePath, declModuleDirectory: signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(func.sourceFilePath), nameLine: func.nameLine, nameColumn: func.nameColumn))
	end 'eachFunc'
end 'seedFunctions'

// `Owner.method` where `Owner` is a declared struct or enum. The owner is split off the LAST dot, so a
// namespace-qualified free function (`api.helper`) is only a method if `api` is itself a type name.
function namesAMethodOnATrackedType(signatures ProgramSignatures, qualifiedName ByteArray) returns bool
	return match splitQualifiedName(qualifiedName) 'split'
		notQualified gives false
		parts(owner, _) gives signatures.containsStruct(owner) or signatures.containsEnum(owner)
	end 'split'
end 'namesAMethodOnATrackedType'

// ⭐ **TYPES ARE SEEDED FROM THE PARSE ARTIFACTS, NOT FROM THE LAYOUT REGISTRIES, BECAUSE THE POSITION
// LIVES THERE.** `StructLayout` and `EnumLayout` carry a `declFilePath` and no name position, and that is
// a DELIBERATE design this pass must not undo: `TypeNameDecl`'s own header records why one array in source
// order beats a position added to each of the four layout types (which of a file's `type Box` and
// `typealias Box` came second is a fact no single registry holds). So the walk is per file, in source
// order, and the tier is looked up per name.
function seedTypes(project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, userFiles FilePathArray, tracked TrackedDecls) throws CompileError
	for path in userFiles 'eachFile'
		let artifact = try queryParseOps(project, path: path)
		for decl in artifact.typeNameDecls 'eachTypeName'
			seedOneTypeName(signatures, decl: decl, tracked: tracked)
		end 'eachTypeName'
	end 'eachFile'
end 'seedTypes'

function seedOneTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, decl TypeNameDecl, tracked TrackedDecls)
	if isSynthesizedName(decl.name) 'compilerOwned'
		return
	end 'compilerOwned'

	let visibility = declaredTypeVisibility(signatures, decl: decl)
	if not tierIsAudited(visibility) 'narrowEnoughAlready'
		return
	end 'narrowEnoughAlready'

	tracked.add(TrackedDecl.create(TrackedDeclKind.trackedType, key: decl.name, displayName: String.from(decl.name), noun: typeDeclNoun(decl.kind), visibility: visibility, declFilePath: decl.declFilePath, declModuleDirectory: signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(decl.declFilePath), nameLine: decl.nameLine, nameColumn: decl.nameColumn))
end 'seedOneTypeName'

// The tier a type name was declared with, asked of whichever registry holds that kind. A kind whose
// registry has no entry answers `file`, which the caller reads as "nothing to audit" — that is the honest
// answer for a declaration the fold dropped, not a sentinel.
function declaredTypeVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, decl TypeNameDecl) returns Visibility
	match decl.kind 'kind'
		structType then return declaredStructVisibility(signatures, name: decl.name)
		enumType then return declaredEnumVisibility(signatures, name: decl.name)
		unionType then return declaredEnumVisibility(signatures, name: decl.name)
		interfaceType then return Visibility.file
		rangedAlias then return declaredAliasVisibility(signatures, decl: decl)
		functionAlias then return Visibility.file
		genericAlias then return Visibility.file
		tupleAlias then return Visibility.file
	end 'kind'
end 'declaredTypeVisibility'

function declaredStructVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, name ByteArray) returns Visibility
	return match signatures.structOf(name) 'lookup'
		declared(layout) gives layout.visibility
		undeclared gives Visibility.file
	end 'lookup'
end 'declaredStructVisibility'

function declaredEnumVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, name ByteArray) returns Visibility
	return match signatures.enumOf(name) 'lookup'
		declared(layout) gives layout.visibility
		undeclared gives Visibility.file
	end 'lookup'
end 'declaredEnumVisibility'

function declaredAliasVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, decl TypeNameDecl) returns Visibility
	return match signatures.aliasOf(decl.name, readerFilePath: decl.declFilePath) 'lookup'
		declared(alias) gives alias.visibility
		undeclared gives Visibility.file
	end 'lookup'
end 'declaredAliasVisibility'

// The word the diagnostic calls a type declaration, matching the reference compiler's vocabulary: a
// struct, enum or union is a "type" and an alias is a "typealias".
function typeDeclNoun(kind TypeDeclKind) returns String
	return match kind 'kind'
		structType gives "type"
		enumType gives "type"
		unionType gives "type"
		interfaceType gives "type"
		rangedAlias gives "typealias"
		functionAlias gives "typealias"
		genericAlias gives "typealias"
		tupleAlias gives "typealias"
	end 'kind'
end 'typeDeclNoun'

function seedBindings(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.topLevelDeclCount() 'eachDecl'
		let decl = signatures.declAt(i)
		if not tierIsAudited(decl.visibility) 'narrowEnoughAlready'
			continue
		end 'narrowEnoughAlready'

		if isSynthesizedName(decl.name) 'compilerOwned'
			continue
		end 'compilerOwned'

		tracked.add(TrackedDecl.create(TrackedDeclKind.trackedBinding, key: decl.name, displayName: String.from(decl.name), noun: "variable" if decl.mutable else "constant", visibility: decl.visibility, declFilePath: decl.declFilePath, declModuleDirectory: signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(decl.declFilePath), nameLine: decl.nameLine, nameColumn: decl.nameColumn))
	end 'eachDecl'
end 'seedBindings'

// ── Reference collection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ⭐⭐ **EVERY REFERENCE IS READ OFF WHAT THE RESOLUTION ALREADY PRODUCED — nothing here re-derives what a
// name means.** That is `DeadGlobalElimination`'s discipline and it is adopted for its reason: a use
// resolves local → capture → top-level, and re-deriving that order has produced a silent wrong answer
// every time something tried. So a call is a `call`/`tryCall`/`asyncCall`/`functionRef` op's own callee
// name, a stored global is a `globalAddr`'s own label, and a type is an id the type layer already interned.
//
// ⚠ **WHAT STANDS IN FOR v1'S `livenessRoots`:** nothing needs to. v1 pins witness-table entries and
// function-backed enum case targets by hand because its IR loses the edge; shv2 emits a `functionRef` for
// a function VALUE, so the same functions are reached by the ordinary walk below.
function collectReferences(module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for func in module.functions 'eachFunc'
		let readerFilePath = func.sourceFilePath
		if readerFilePath.toString().isEmpty() 'synthesizedReaderNamesNothingAnAuthorWrote'
			continue
		end 'synthesizedReaderNamesNothingAnAuthorWrote'

		let readerModuleDirectory = signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(readerFilePath)
		noteSignatureTypes(func, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
		noteBodyReferences(module, func: func, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'eachFunc'

	noteCrossFileConstantReads(signatures, tracked: tracked)
	noteTopLevelInitializerCallees(signatures, tracked: tracked)
end 'collectReferences'

// A declared signature names types in the DECLARING file — its parameters, its return and its `throws`.
// That is a reference like any other: `function consumeAlias(value UnusedAlias)` is what keeps
// `UnusedAlias` alive for its own file, and `specs/unused-export.md`'s
// `error.unused-exported-typealias` is the case that pins it (the alias IS named, in-file, and is still
// E3092 because nothing OUTSIDE names it).
function noteSignatureTypes(func IrFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	for paramType in func.maxonParamTypes 'eachParam'
		noteSignatureType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: paramType, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'eachParam'

	// A `void` return names no type. `unresolved` is the arm the walk below already drops, so it stands in
	// for "no type" rather than a second shape of "nothing" invented here.
	let returned = match func.maxonReturnType 'ret'
		value(t) gives t
		void gives MaxonType.unresolved
	end 'ret'
	noteSignatureType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: returned, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)

	noteThrowsType(func, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)

	// ⛔⛔ **`IrFunction.valueNameIds` IS DELIBERATELY NOT READ HERE, AND THE ATTEMPT PRODUCED A WRONG
	// ANSWER.** It is the obvious source for "what named types does this body mention?" — a dense
	// per-SSA-value column of interned `TypeNameId`s. But it is dense by ValueId over a column that
	// includes slots no value in THIS function occupies, and such a slot carries a leftover tag and a
	// leftover id rather than the `UnnamedTypeId` filler its header describes.
	//
	// **MEASURED:** `function main() returns ExitCode / return entry()` — a body naming no type at all,
	// with no parameters — reports `v0 tag=named nameId=1`, and project-global id 1 was whatever alias
	// happened to intern first. So `export typealias UnusedAlias`, used only as an IN-FILE parameter
	// type, was credited with a read from `app/main.maxon` and `specs/unused-export.md`'s
	// `error.unused-exported-typealias` compiled CLEAN instead of reporting E3092. Gating on the parallel
	// `valueTags` does not cure it: the leftover slot's TAG is `named` too. Renaming the aliases moved the
	// false read to whichever one then held id 1, which is what identified it.
	//
	// ⇒ The coverage it was reaching for — "another file names this type" — is served precisely, and
	// without any interner id, by `noteQualifiedOwner` on the callee walk: a file that uses a type
	// CALLS something on it (`LocalPoint.origin()`, `p.sum()`), and the owner half of that qualified
	// callee name is the reference.
end 'noteSignatureTypes'

function noteBodyReferences(module MaxonModule, func IrFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'eachBlock'
		let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("checkUnusedExports: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")
		for opIdx in block.opRefs 'eachOp'
			let op = try module.ops.get(opIdx) otherwise panic("checkUnusedExports: opRef {opIdx} not in module.ops")
			noteOpReferences(signatures, tracked: tracked, op: op, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
		end 'eachOp'
	end 'eachBlock'
end 'noteBodyReferences'

// A `throws E` clause names `E` in the declaring file. Split out because a match arm is ONE statement,
// and `throwsClauseName` already answers "is there one?" by throwing rather than by a second predicate.
function noteThrowsType(func IrFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	let errorName = try throwsClauseName(func.throwsTypeName) otherwise return
	noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: errorName.toByteArray(), readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
end 'noteThrowsType'

// ⭐⭐ **CALLING A FUNCTION USES ITS DECLARED ERROR TYPE, AND THE CALLER'S FILE IS WHERE THAT USE HAPPENS.**
// `try risky(9) otherwise (e)` binds `e` to `risky`'s declared error union without the caller ever writing
// the name, and it was MEASURED reporting E3092 against the very type the case exists to pass across a file
// boundary.
//
// ⛔ **THE RETURN TYPE IS NOT ASKED HERE, AND THIS HEADER CLAIMED IT WAS FOR THE WHOLE LIFE OF THE FILE**
// (found BATCH43, by the program the claim predicts: `let a = build()` then `a.n`, with `build` and its
// record declared together in another file, reported E3092 against that record and E4006 once the advice was
// taken). It is not asked because it is not this pass's to derive: a value's type matters here only when the
// reader reaches INTO it, and the lines that decide THAT are `Parser.requireFieldAccessible` and
// `Parser.emitEnumTagOf`, whose answers arrive as `FileParseArtifact.memberAccessedTypeNames`. Reading
// `returnTypeOf` as well would credit every caller of every factory with its record whether or not the caller
// ever opened one — three families of correct findings, deleted (see `collectFileTypeReferences`), plus
// `unused-export/error.unused-exported-union-nothing-outside-reaches`, whose whole subject is a file that
// receives a union value and never opens it.
function noteCalleeSignature(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, callee ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	let errorName = try throwsClauseName(signatures.throwsOf(callee)) otherwise return
	noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: errorName.toByteArray(), readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
end 'noteCalleeSignature'

function noteOpReferences(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, op MaxonOp, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	// `direct` and `functionValue` are one answer here: both name a function this file reaches, and the
	// distinction between them is about whether a RESOLVER may rewrite the name, which this pass never does.
	if maxonOpCalleeKind(op) != MaxonCalleeKind.noCallee 'namesACallee'
		noteFunctionName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: maxonOpCalleeName(op), readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
		noteCalleeSignature(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: maxonOpCalleeName(op), readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'namesACallee'

	if maxonOpNamesAGlobalLabel(op) 'namesAStoredGlobal'
		noteGlobalLabel(signatures, tracked: tracked, label: maxonOpGlobalLabelName(op), readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'namesAStoredGlobal'
end 'noteOpReferences'

// ⭐⭐ **THE TWO SETS EACH FILE'S OWN PARSE RECORDED — the names it WROTE, and the types it reached a MEMBER
// of without writing anything.** Neither survives anywhere else, and the check is wrong without either.
//
// **WRITTEN NAMES** are the one source that survives ERASURE. A ranged typealias in a signature is `integer`
// by the time any pass sees it (MEASURED: `scoreOf(s Score)` declared in another file leaves
// `maxonParamTypes` holding `integer` with `UnnamedTypeId`), so reading declared types alone reports a
// genuinely-used `export typealias` as E3092 — a wrong answer. The parser already records this set for
// E3062, which asks the same question one scope narrower ("did this FILE use its own alias?"), so the answer
// is shared rather than re-derived.
//
// ⭐⭐ **MEMBER-ACCESSED TYPES ARE THE RESOLVER'S OWN ANSWER TO THIS PASS'S QUESTION, AND WITHOUT THEM THE
// TWO DIAGNOSTICS CONTRADICTED EACH OTHER (BATCH43).** `for it in h.items` then `it.n` requires `Item`
// VISIBLE and never spells it: the transitive walk below reaches `Holder`'s field type `ItemArray` and stops
// at the alias, so E3092 told the author to drop an `export` that E4006 then refused the access without —
// a program with no legal spelling. `Parser.requireFieldAccessible` is the line that decides that
// visibility question, so it is the line that records it; this pass ASKS the resolver instead of walking the
// type graph a second, weaker way.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THE SAME CLASS, THIRD INSTANCE: AN ENUM OR UNION REACHED THROUGH A `match` (BATCH43).** `match
// classify(42)` on another file's `union Answer` spells its CASES (`small`, `big(n)`) and never its TYPE, as
// `s.ordinal` spells a member and an interpolation hole spells nothing — so nothing written reaches
// `usedTypeNames` and the transitive walk has no field to follow. E3092 said to drop the `export`, and with it
// dropped the BOOTSTRAP CRASHED on the identical program (E9001 in `SetupMatchScrutinee`): advice with no
// legal spelling under EITHER compiler. `Parser.emitEnumTagOf` — the one line that reads a tag out of a value
// of a declared enum — records it, for `requireFieldAccessible`'s reason and through its channel.
//
// ⚠ **IT IS NOT "EVERY TYPE STRUCTURALLY REACHABLE FROM ONE THIS FILE NAMES", AND THAT DISTINCTION IS
// MEASURED.** A reader that holds a `Crate with Item`, a `function(Payload) returns …` or a `(Elem, Integer)`
// without ever reaching INTO one compiles perfectly well once the `export` is dropped — verified on all
// three — so crediting them would delete three families of correct findings. What earns a credit is a
// visibility the resolver actually demanded.
function collectFileTypeReferences(project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, userFiles FilePathArray, tracked TrackedDecls) throws CompileError
	for path in userFiles 'eachFile'
		let artifact = try queryParseOps(project, path: path)
		let readerModuleDirectory = signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(path)
		noteEveryTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, names: artifact.usedTypeNames, readerFilePath: path, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
		noteEveryTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, names: artifact.memberAccessedTypeNames, readerFilePath: path, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'eachFile'
end 'collectFileTypeReferences'

// Both of a file's recorded name sets are credited the same way — the two differ in what they MEAN, not in
// what a reference to one of their names does, so the crediting is written once.
function noteEveryTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, names UsedTypeNameSet, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	for name in names 'eachName'
		noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'eachName'
end 'noteEveryTypeName'

// v1's `crossFileConstReads`, in shv2's spelling — see `ProgramSignatures.notedConstantValue` for why an
// inlined constant cannot be found in the IR at all.
function noteCrossFileConstantReads(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.crossFileConstantReadCount() 'eachRead'
		let read = signatures.crossFileConstantReadAt(i)
		noteBindingName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: read.name, readerFilePath: read.readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(read.readerFilePath))
	end 'eachRead'
end 'noteCrossFileConstantReads'

// ── Matching a reference to a seeded declaration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

function noteFunctionName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	noteQualifiedOwner(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	if let claimants = try tracked.functionIndex.get(name) 'tracked'
		noteEveryClaimant(tracked, claimants: claimants, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'tracked'
end 'noteFunctionName'

// ⭐ **A CALL TO `Owner.member` IS A REFERENCE TO `Owner`.** This is how one file names another file's
// TYPE in practice — `LocalPoint.origin()`, `p.sum()`, `Status.fromRawValue(…)` — and it is read off the
// callee name the resolution already produced, so it needs no interner id and cannot collide the way
// `IrFunction.valueNameIds` did (see `noteSignatureTypes`). A callee whose owner half is not a tracked
// type simply matches nothing: a namespace-qualified free function (`api.helper`) resolves against the
// FUNCTION index above, not this one.
function noteQualifiedOwner(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, callee ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	match splitQualifiedName(callee) 'split'
		notQualified then return
		parts(owner, _) then noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: owner, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'split'
end 'noteQualifiedOwner'

// ⭐⭐ **USING A TYPE USES THE TYPES IT IS MADE OF, AND WITHOUT THAT THE CHECK REPORTS A WRONG ANSWER.**
// A file can depend on a type without ever writing its name: `let c = Gate.make().c` names `Gate` and
// consumes a `Color`, and `try f() otherwise …` catches a `Woe` its file never spells. MEASURED — those
// two shapes were 9 of the corpus's failures, every one of them a spec whose SUBJECT is that the
// cross-file reference works. v1 propagates the same way and for the same reason
// (`UnusedExportCheck.propagateFieldTypeUse`, memoized by `UseVisited`).
//
// The walk is bounded by `visited`, which is what makes a self-referential type (`type Node { next as
// Node }`) terminate rather than recurse forever.
function noteTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	var visited = VisitedTypeNameSet.create()
	noteTypeNameTransitively(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
end 'noteTypeName'

function noteTypeNameTransitively(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	if visited.contains(name) 'alreadyWalked'
		return
	end 'alreadyWalked'
	visited.insert(name)

	if let claimants = try tracked.typeIndex.get(name) 'tracked'
		noteEveryClaimant(tracked, claimants: claimants, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'tracked'

	// A type this pass does not TRACK is still walked through: a file-private struct may hold a field of
	// an exported type, and a reader that reaches the one reaches the other.
	noteStructFieldTypes(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
	noteEnumPayloadTypes(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
end 'noteTypeNameTransitively'

function noteStructFieldTypes(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	match signatures.structOf(name) 'lookup'
		undeclared then return
		declared(layout) then noteComponentTypes(signatures, tracked: tracked, types: layout.fieldTypes, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
	end 'lookup'
end 'noteStructFieldTypes'

function noteEnumPayloadTypes(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	match signatures.enumOf(name) 'lookup'
		undeclared then return
		declared(layout) then noteEveryPayloadType(signatures, tracked: tracked, layout: layout, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
	end 'lookup'
end 'noteEnumPayloadTypes'

function noteEveryPayloadType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, layout EnumLayout, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	for payloadFields in layout.casePayloads 'eachCase'
		for field in payloadFields 'eachField'
			noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: field.declaredType, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
		end 'eachField'
	end 'eachCase'
end 'noteEveryPayloadType'

function noteComponentTypes(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, types MaxonTypeArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	for fieldType in types 'eachField'
		noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: fieldType, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
	end 'eachField'
end 'noteComponentTypes'

// ⛔ **`typeNameIdOf` IS NOT A NAME-ID GETTER FOR EVERY ARM, AND USING IT AS ONE CONFLATES TWO ID
// SPACES.** Its `typeParameter` and `genericInstance` arms return a type-parameter DIGEST and a
// `GenericInstanceId` — both ride the same column so the value round-trips, but neither indexes the type
// NAME interner. Resolving one through `typeNameOf` asks the wrong table and answers with whatever name
// happens to occupy that slot, which is the same shape of defect `IrFunction.valueNameIds` produced.
//
// ⭐ And a generic instance's TYPE ARGUMENTS are references in their own right: `Array with Item` names
// `Item`, and nothing else in this walk would ever reach it.
function noteComponentType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, type MaxonType, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	match type 'type'
		named(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
		structRef(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
		interfaceRef(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
		function(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
		genericInstance(id) then noteInstanceArgs(signatures, tracked: tracked, id: id, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
		// A type PARAMETER's id is a digest, not a name, and the parameter itself names no declaration.
		typeParameter then return
		boolean to float then return
		exitCode to unresolved then return
		string then return
		character then return
	end 'type'
end 'noteComponentType'

function noteInstanceArgs(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, id GenericInstanceId, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	for position in 0 upto signatures.genericInstanceArgCount(id) 'eachArg'
		noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: signatures.substitutedInstanceArg(id, position: position), readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
	end 'eachArg'
end 'noteInstanceArgs'

function noteComponentTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, nameId TypeNameId, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String, visited VisitedTypeNameSet)
	if nameId == UnnamedTypeId 'namesNothing'
		return
	end 'namesNothing'

	let componentName = try signatures.typeNameOf(nameId) otherwise return
	noteTypeNameTransitively(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: componentName, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
end 'noteComponentTypeName'

function noteBindingName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	noteQualifiedOwner(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	if let claimants = try tracked.bindingIndex.get(name) 'tracked'
		noteEveryClaimant(tracked, claimants: claimants, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'tracked'
end 'noteBindingName'

// A stored global is reached by its `.data` LABEL, which is what the op carries; the seed is keyed by
// source name. The arena holds both, so the label is translated here rather than the seed being keyed by
// something a `let` does not have (an immutable binding has no label at all — see `TopLevelDecl.dataLabel`).
// A label no declaration owns names nothing this pass tracks — the honest answer for a `.data` slot the
// compiler minted for itself, and the same answer the scan's fall-through gave.
function noteGlobalLabel(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, label ByteArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	let index = try tracked.globalLabels.get(label) otherwise return
	let decl = signatures.declAt(index)
	noteBindingName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: decl.name, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	noteSlotType(signatures, tracked: tracked, index: index, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
end 'noteGlobalLabel'

// ⭐⭐ **THE CLASSIFICATION RULE, AND ITS ONE DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM WHAT `module` MEANS.** A reader in
// the SAME DIRECTORY as the declaration counts as OUTSIDE its module subtree, even though
// `Visibility.module` would make the declaration visible to it. That is v1's rule
// (`UnusedExportCheck.recordRead`) and it is not an oversight: without it, every flat two-file program
// would be told to downgrade its `export`s to `module`, which is advice about a program's directory
// layout rather than about its visibility. Only a STRICTLY NESTED reader keeps a declaration
// downgradable — which is why the equality case is excluded here rather than left to
// `moduleDirectoryContains`, whose own answer includes it.
function noteRead(tracked TrackedDecls, index TrackedDeclIndex, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	var decl = tracked.at(index)
	// Both spellings are taken ONCE and reused by the two tests below — the same-file test already needed
	// both, and this runs at every credit the walk makes.
	let readerPath = readerFilePath.toString()
	let declPath = decl.declFilePath.toString()
	if declPath.equals(readerPath) 'itsOwnFile'
		return
	end 'itsOwnFile'

	// ⭐⭐ **A LIBRARY FILE CANNOT NAME AN AUTHOR'S DECLARATION — A CREDIT THAT SAYS OTHERWISE IS A
	// MONOMORPH'S SIGNATURE, NOT A REFERENCE.** `stdlib/` is compiled with no knowledge whatever of user
	// code, so no line in it can mention `type Item`; what the walk actually met is `ArrayIterator.create`
	// INSTANTIATED over the author's element type, whose `sourceFilePath` is `stdlib/Array.maxon` because
	// that is where its body was written. The instantiation was demanded by an author's file, and that file
	// is credited on its own wherever it genuinely reaches the type.
	//
	// ⛔ **IT SUPPRESSED TRUE FINDINGS, AND IT DID SO UNPREDICTABLY.** MEASURED (BATCH43): two three-file
	// programs differing only in whether the READING file declared its own `typealias Count` got different
	// answers for the same `export type Item` — one E3092, one clean — because the monomorphized iterator's
	// signature mentioned `Item` in one and not in the other. It also made the E3093 half of this pass
	// unfalsifiable: every route by which an outside file reaches a container's ELEMENT type runs through a
	// library generic, so the finding could not fire on any of them.
	//
	// ⚠ **ONE DIRECTION ONLY.** A library file reading a LIBRARY declaration is an ordinary reference, and it
	// is what keeps `stdlib/String.maxon`'s six `module` declarations audited (see this file's header).
	if tracked.libraryFiles.contains(readerPath) and not tracked.libraryFiles.contains(declPath) 'aLibraryBodyNamedNothingTheAuthorWrote'
		return
	end 'aLibraryBodyNamedNothingTheAuthorWrote'

	decl.sawOutsideFile = true

	let strictlyNested = moduleDirectoryContains(decl.declModuleDirectory, inner: readerModuleDirectory) and not decl.declModuleDirectory.equals(readerModuleDirectory)
	if not strictlyNested 'outsideTheSubtree'
		decl.sawOutsideModule = true
	end 'outsideTheSubtree'

	try tracked.entries.set(index, value: decl) otherwise panic("checkUnusedExports: entries.set OOB at {index} — the index came from this seed")
end 'noteRead'

// ── Emission ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// In DECLARATION order, which is the order the seed was built in — see `TrackedDecls`.
function emitDiagnostics(project Project, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto tracked.entries.count() 'eachTracked'
		emitOne(project, decl: tracked.at(i))
	end 'eachTracked'
end 'emitDiagnostics'

function emitOne(project Project, decl TrackedDecl)
	match decl.visibility 'tier'
		file then panic("checkUnusedExports: a `file` declaration reached emit ({decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}') — `tierIsAudited` filters it at seed time")
		public then panic("checkUnusedExports: a `public` declaration reached emit ({decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}') — `tierIsAudited` filters it at seed time, which is the whole of the exemption")
		module then emitForModuleTier(project, decl: decl)
		global then emitForGlobalTier(project, decl: decl)
	end 'tier'
end 'emitOne'

function emitForModuleTier(project Project, decl TrackedDecl)
	if not decl.sawOutsideFile 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'
		reportPositioned(project, code: ErrorCode.semanticUnusedModuleSymbol, message: "module {decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}' is never referenced outside its declaring file", line: decl.nameLine, column: decl.nameColumn, filePath: decl.declFilePath)
	end 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'
end 'emitForModuleTier'

function emitForGlobalTier(project Project, decl TrackedDecl)
	if not decl.sawOutsideFile 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'
		reportPositioned(project, code: ErrorCode.semanticUnusedExportedSymbol, message: "exported {decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}' is never referenced outside its declaring file", line: decl.nameLine, column: decl.nameColumn, filePath: decl.declFilePath)
		return
	end 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'

	if not decl.sawOutsideModule 'onlyItsOwnSubtreeNamesIt'
		reportPositioned(project, code: ErrorCode.semanticExportableAsModule, message: "exported {decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}' is only referenced inside its declaring module subtree; consider 'module' visibility", line: decl.nameLine, column: decl.nameColumn, filePath: decl.declFilePath)
	end 'onlyItsOwnSubtreeNamesIt'
end 'emitForGlobalTier'

// ⭐ **A TOP-LEVEL INITIALIZER'S CALLS, ATTRIBUTED TO THE FILE THAT WROTE THEM.** `var a = Outer.build()`
// is lowered into the synthesized `__module_init`, whose `sourceFilePath` is empty — so the body walk
// skips it and the call is invisible. Asked per DECLARATION instead, which is what carries the declaring
// file, rather than off `globalInitCallees()`, whose flat list has lost it. MEASURED on
// `top-level-factory-globals/factory-returning-a-record-declared-in-another-file`.
function noteTopLevelInitializerCallees(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.topLevelDeclCount() 'eachDecl'
		let decl = signatures.declAt(i)
		noteOneInitializersCallees(signatures, tracked: tracked, decl: decl)
	end 'eachDecl'
end 'noteTopLevelInitializerCallees'

function noteOneInitializersCallees(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, decl TopLevelDecl)
	match signatures.declScopeInitializerCall(decl) 'initializer'
		none then return
		calls(callees) then noteEveryInitializerCallee(signatures, tracked: tracked, callees: callees, readerFilePath: decl.declFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(decl.declFilePath))
	end 'initializer'
end 'noteOneInitializersCallees'

function noteEveryInitializerCallee(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, callees ByteArrayArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	for callee in callees 'eachCallee'
		noteFunctionName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: callee, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
		noteCalleeSignature(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: callee, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'eachCallee'
end 'noteEveryInitializerCallee'

// A declared signature type, walked with the same arm-correct rules the component walk uses — so a
// parameter typed `Array with Item` credits `Item` exactly as a field of that type would.
function noteSignatureType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, type MaxonType, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	var visited = VisitedTypeNameSet.create()
	noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: type, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory, visited: visited)
end 'noteSignatureType'

// Every declaration wearing the referenced name — see `TrackedDeclIndexMap` for why there can be more
// than one and why crediting all of them is the safe direction.
function noteEveryClaimant(tracked TrackedDecls, claimants TrackedDeclIndexArray, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	for at in claimants 'eachClaimant'
		noteRead(tracked, index: at, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'eachClaimant'
end 'noteEveryClaimant'

// ⭐ **REFERENCING A BINDING USES ITS TYPE** — see `ProgramSignatures.globalSlotType` for the measurement.
// The slot type is walked with the same transitive rules a field type is, so naming `db` reaches
// `Database`, the `EntryMap` it holds and the `Entry` inside that.
function noteSlotType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, index TopLevelDeclIndex, readerFilePath FilePath, readerModuleDirectory String)
	match signatures.globalSlotType(index) 'slot'
		notFound then return
		found(_, valueType, _) then noteSignatureType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: valueType, readerFilePath: readerFilePath, readerModuleDirectory: readerModuleDirectory)
	end 'slot'
end 'noteSlotType'
